<objective>
Execute {tool_name} operations using the `{tool_name}` CLI. All {tool_name} interactions should use this CLI.
</objective>

<quick_start>
The `{tool_name}` CLI follows this pattern:
```bash
{tool_name} <command-group> <action> [arguments] [options]
```

{common_commands}
</quick_start>

<essential_principles>
<principle name="Usage Reference">
**MANDATORY: Consult `usage.json` before executing ANY `{tool_name}` command.**
This file contains complete command syntax, all arguments, all options, and usage instructions for every command. Never guess at command syntax.
</principle>

<principle name="AI Instruction Results">
After every `{tool_name}` command, inspect stdout. If it is JSON with `type: "ai_instruction"` and `schema_version: "1.0"`, follow the instruction object as the next task instead of summarizing it as ordinary command output. Use the allowed tools, context, constraints, and success criteria in the payload. Run `verification_commands` or `follow_up_commands` only after completing the instructed AI work; they are not required commands for performing the handoff.
</principle>

